# PC2 cluster only — copy to local.env (gitignored) and run with --pc2 or C2HLS_SITE=pc2.
# Without --pc2 the repo uses the team's default server paths and ignores local.env.
#
#   cp local.env.example local.env    # template stays in repo; local.env is gitignored
#   ./c2hls.py --pc2 --bench nw

# --- Scratch / temp (in-repo, gitignored) ------------------------------------
# On --pc2, defaults to <repo>/c2hls_tmp/ (created on first run). Not $HOME.
# C2HLS_TMP_ROOT=/other/writable/path

# --- Xilinx / Vitis / XRT (PC2 Otus modules + U280 platform) -----------------
# scripts/pc2/setup_vitis_env.sh loads PC2_COMPUTE_MODULES, swaps to the U280
# shell, then sources the paths below. Used by setup_emu_env.sh on --pc2.
#
# C2HLS_VITIS_SETTINGS=/opt/software/FPGA/Xilinx/Vitis/2023.2/settings64.sh
# C2HLS_XRT_SETUP=/opt/software/FPGA/Xilinx/XRT/xrt_2.16/setup.sh
# C2HLS_PLATFORM_REPO_PATHS=/opt/software/FPGA/Xilinx/platforms/xilinx_u280_gen3x16_xdma_1_202211_1
# C2HLS_DEVICE_PLATFORM=xilinx_u280_gen3x16_xdma_1_202211_1
# PC2_COMPUTE_MODULES=fpga xilinx/xrt/2.16
# PC2_COMPUTE_U280_SWAP_TO=xilinx/u280/xdma_202211_1
#
# PC2 pilot: csynth + csim only (no cosim / hw_emu). Team server defaults unchanged.
# C2HLS_RUN_COSIM=0
# C2HLS_COSIM_REQUIRED=0
# C2HLS_REFERENCE_COSIM=0
# C2HLS_HW_EMU_FINAL=0

# --- Upstream benchmark sources (optional — only for prepare_benchmarks) -----
# C2HLS_RODINIA_HLS_DIR=
# C2HLS_RODINIA_NOVA_DIR=
# C2HLS_ML4ACCEL_DIR=
# C2HLS_ML4ACCEL_ROOT=

# --- LLM / vLLM (PC2 self-hosted on gpu_h100) --------------------------------
# Local models (Devstral, Nemotron, etc.) use OPENAI_BASE_URL, not the hosted
# OpenAI API. c2hls.py reads OPENAI_BASE_URL for non-gpt-* model ids.
#
# C2HLS_MODEL=mistralai/Devstral-2-123B-Instruct-2512
# OPENAI_API_KEY=EMPTY
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://gpu-node:8000/v1    # set by scripts/pc2/compute_worker
#
# GPU node: scripts/pc2/setup_vllm_env.sh loads PC2_GPU_MODULES, then activates
# PC2_VLLM_VENV. PC2 modules provide CUDA/Python only — vLLM is not on PATH.
# REQUIRED for scripts/pc2/gpu_serve.sbatch.sh unless you set PC2_LLM_SERVE_CMD
# to a custom launch (e.g. multi-node Ray + vLLM) or run serving separately.
# PC2_GPU_MODULES=lang system CUDA/12.6.0 Python/3.11.5-GCCcore-13.2.0
PC2_VLLM_VENV=/scratch/hpc-prf-llmfpga/asa582/projects/devstral2/.venv
#
# API key files (only if you use Claude/OpenAI cloud APIs instead):
# C2HLS_CLAUDE_KEY_FILE=
# C2HLS_OPENAI_KEY_FILE=

# --- Python interpreter (optional) -------------------------------------------
# C2HLS_PYTHON=python3

# --- PC2 supervised batch (scripts/pc2/start_session.sh) ---------------------
# 1) GPU queues on gpu_h100 → vLLM serve when allocated
# 2) Compute submitted after GPU RUNNING (Slurm after:gpu_job)
# 3) Compute worker waits for LLM health, then runs c2hls with OPENAI_BASE_URL
#
# PC2_GPU_PARTITION=gpu_h100
# PC2_COMPUTE_PARTITION=fpga
# PC2_WALLTIME=1-00:00:00
# PC2_COMPUTE_LLM_WAIT_SEC=7200
# PC2_LLM_MODEL=mistralai/Devstral-2-123B-Instruct-2512
# PC2_LLM_PORT=8000
# PC2_GPU_GPUS=1
# PC2_VLLM_TENSOR_PARALLEL_SIZE=1
# PC2_VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS=--served-model-name mistralai/Devstral-2-123B-Instruct-2512
# PC2_LLM_SERVE_CMD=              # override default vllm serve (e.g. multi-node Ray)
# PC2_WORKER_CMD=python3 scripts/pc2/run_flash_noskills_batch.py --pc2
# PC2_WORKER_CMD=python3 c2hls.py --pc2 --bench nw --multistep
# Or standalone: sbatch scripts/pc2/flash_noskills_batch.sbatch.sh

# --- Optional: skills config override ----------------------------------------
# C2HLS_SKILLS_PATH=hls_full_optimization_skills_schema_1_1_package/skills.json
